### Two adaptations vs e1865fee (sustainability-driven, env diverged)
1. **Async SlayzoneDb + warmed-cache SettingsService now exist.** e1865fee's raw
   `getSetting/setSetting` free-fns (sync better-sqlite3) would bypass SettingsService's
   write-through → stale `getCached()` (idle-close sweep, warmed keys). So router
   get/set/getAll route through `SettingsService.forDatabase(ctx.db)` — verified the
   SAME warmed singleton: app does `SettingsService.forDatabase(db)` + `startTrpcServer({db})`
   with one `db`; ws-server `baseContext={db}` → `ctx.db` === warmed handle. Cache coherent.
2. **`src/main/` not `src/electron/`.** Moved electron-free `service.ts` → `src/server/`
   (matches projects/task-terminals convention); `/main` barrel re-exports it → zero churn
   to the only external importer (app/main).

